    "# Validating explanations on a pediatric SFCN (public Calgary controls)\n",
    "\n",
    "**One line.** Das et al. (2024) flagged their explainability as *preliminary* - a single coarse Grad-CAM map, with only one of four named regions tested statistically. This notebook takes that stated limitation and builds the rigorous version: a pre-specified battery that tests which explanation methods are **faithful**, **stable across methods**, and **anatomically valid** on *their exact model class*.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Same model, proxy task.** We use the *same* network they used - the pretrained SFCN (Peng et al., 2021), frozen, six convolutional blocks kept as a feature extractor. The only differences are the small head on top and the label it predicts:\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Das et al. (2024) | This study |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Backbone | Pretrained SFCN, frozen | **Same** pretrained SFCN, frozen |\n",
    "| Head | small dense head → age group | small dense head → **age group** (public label) |\n",
    "| Data | private PAE + public controls | **public controls only** (cohort counts in the README) |\n",
    "\n",
    "Swapping the head's task does **not** invalidate the XAI. Explanation *validity* - faithfulness, the randomized-weight sanity check, cross-method agreement, resolution - is a property of the **method and the architecture**, not of the task. Testing it on a controllable proxy is standard practice (Adebayo et al. 2018; Siegel et al. 2025).\n",
    "\n",
    "**What this does and does not show.**\n",
    "\n",
    "| Claim | This notebook |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Which XAI methods are trustworthy on the SFCN | **Yes - the deliverable** |\n",
    "| Grad-CAM over-resolves / methods disagree / which fail sanity | **Yes - the headline** |\n",
    "| Anything about alcohol exposure, FASD, PAE | **No - needs the private cohort** |\n",
    "| Reproducing the paper's 85-88% accuracy | **No - that was the PAE task** |\n",
    "\n",
    "The second column is the **next stage** and the reason to collaborate - not a gap in this work.\n"
   ]
  },
