    "## Before you run: status and checks\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data.** OSF fork `5kz2p` (the original `axz5r` storage is empty). T1 scans are at `T1_Dataset/<PreschoolID>/<session>/<scan>.nii.gz`. Labels come from the `All_Datasets` sheet of `Calgary_Preschool_Dataset_Updated_*.xlsx` (age and sex).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Known issue (fixed).** The first downloader skipped eleven children, whose spreadsheet scan IDs (for example `PS1064-1`) do not match the file names (`PS1064101`). `code/fetch_extra_scans.py` adds them. The manifest now lists 96 children. Two of the eleven added scans failed visual QC on the first run (PS0536101, PS1432101). Both were rerun and pass; see `results/preprocessing.md`.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Checks on any new run.**\n",
    "1. SFCN `state_dict` keys: the loader raises if any `feature_extractor.*` key does not match.\n",
    "2. Registration: open the saved QC slices for 2 to 3 scans. Poor registration gives poor explanations.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Compute.** Run the modes in order:\n",
    "1. `MODE=\"smoke\"`: 3 scans, every slow setting reduced. Checks that the code runs. Its numbers are not results.\n",
    "2. `MODE=\"pilot\"`: 20 scans with the real settings.\n",
    "3. `MODE=\"full\"`: every child in the manifest.\n",
    "\n",
    "Preprocessing runs on CPU (ANTs). Feature extraction and attributions use the GPU.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Every heavy stage caches to disk**, so a re-run resumes instead of repeating."
